  "final_message": "Refunding a paid invoice should no longer raise the \"no successful payment\" error. I haven't run a refund end to end. The existing 24 tests pass, but they passed before the fix too, so they don't cover this case.\n\n**Root cause:** `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py` called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`. That function expects an invoice id and looks payments up by invoice. Given a customer id, it found nothing, so nothing was refunded and the function raised `InvalidStateError`. The fix passes `invoice_id` instead.\n\nAn invoice paid partly with account credit would still have been refunded as credit, so the error only hit invoices paid entirely by card.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`.",
